\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The witness edge has 12 double cosets}
\date{2026-11-21}

\p{For the stabilizer of order three in \ref{fdip-0126}, there are
#{6} double cosets of size #{3} and #{6} of size #{9}.
\ref{fdip-012D} therefore gives a preserved space of rank #{12}
for any class-function kernel and any double-coset kernel. The
pairing kernel of \ref{fdip-012F}, applied to the nonzero vector
of \ref{fdip-0126}, is one such double-coset kernel, and its
maximizing set is that stabilizer.}
